    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0737" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003 C 73/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-05-25T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 25—10:34
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>181. Your number 82, May 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d482-f1"/> Identic
                    telegram sent as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Chinese Government having requested that the Commission on
                            Extraterritoriality should meet on November 1, 1923, the representatives
                            of the signatory powers of the treaties of Washington have the honor to
                            inform their Governments that, in view of existing conditions in China,
                            they are of the opinion that the meeting of this Commission should be
                            once more postponed and not convened until they can recommend its
                            assembly.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>This was unanimously adopted by my colleagues at informal conference 24th. I
                    explained, however, that I could not commit myself without instructions from my
                    Government. The telegram would, in my opinion, be endorsed by every member of
                    the diplomatic body.</p>
                <pb facs="0738" n="622" xml:id="pg622"/>
                <p>I share the sentiment expressed with respect to postponement of meeting of
                    Commission from the Chinese point of view, but I thought it possible that you
                    might consider meeting desirable to complete work of Washington Conference. Both
                    British Minister and I opposed a resolution favored by all the others
                    recommending postponement of special surtax conference on the ground that our
                    Governments were in favor of holding it. French Minister stated confidentially
                    that he had learned from private sources that the Washington treaties, though
                    now holding a favorable [place] on the agenda, could not be ratified by French
                    Parliament unless a special personal effort should be made on their behalf by
                    Poincaré.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
